/E (Health and social care are in crisis. We are graduating too few doctors. Rural practices are being shuttered or run down. Patients are waiting too long for critical treatment. Our education systems are little better, with standards falling and Scotland's standing in international large-scale assessments of education having entered a secular decline. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 204 0 R
/E (The cost-of-living crisis continues to strain family finances. The jobs market is illiquid, and many employers are struggling with the taxation burdens placed on them by the state. Too many of our people are finding that full-time work does not pay enough to support a family, and must rely on benefits to pay their bills.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
