286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (Despite the years of union, we have managed to preserve our sense of identity. As a people, we have traditionally put society and community first, not the state or individual. We have a strong sense of place, and of obligation to our neighbours. Many of us remember a time when people routinely left their front doors open. Where neighbours pulled together in a crisis. Where children were free to play on the streets without fear of being accosted.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (Now, people are increasingly leading atomised lives, dominated by mass media and global information technologies. The value of work is being undermined by state policy and by a culture of dependency.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 17 0 R
