289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (Programmes designed to indoctrinate students should be binned, and schools should be staffed by teachers with character, focused on the pursuit of truth, on rigorous academics, and students' welfare. We will end sex education in primary schools, and ban mobile phone use in schools. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (Education should be more rounded. There should be common, merit-based exams at age 16, followed by preparation for university, or vocational education, apprenticeships in the context of the last two years of school. Schools should support a wider range of activities for students, including funded driving lessons. Further education should be put on the same level as higher education, with industry partnerships, and exacting vocational courses leading to well-paying careers.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (Priority in our universities and colleges should be given to young Scots, not overseas students. We should better support parents and homeschooling families, by ensuring that those raising and educating their children at home are not pressured by the benefits system into finding work, and support marriage by ensuring that the basic allowance is fully transferable between parties in a married couple.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
