/P 207 0 R
/E (Community breakdown is the cause of major social problems. Local councils lack a strong connection with local communities. In communitarian Scotland, government should allow communities to take care of themselves. Undercover policing should stop undermining communities, neighbourhoods and families, diminishing the trust central for civil society.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (The Gender Recognition Reform \(GRR\) should be repealed. No woman should feel unsafe using women's safe spaces. Women's safety should be prioritised as a matter of urgency.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
298 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (Our prisons should be humane, focused on rehabilitation. Everyone has a right to a second )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
299 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (chance. Instead, the less prisoners have to do, the more violent they become. There should be no indeterminate sentences, and no orders of lifelong imprisonment, decided on in shady, unaccountable proceedings. We will review the use of Orders for Lifelong Restriction \(OLR\), and replace them with a more just sentencing regime. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
300 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (Scotland has one of the highest incarceration rates in Europe. Many of our communities have been blighted by ineffective government on drugs and drug crime, and undermining our national self-confidence.  With independence, this will change!)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (One in three men, and one in ten women have a criminal record, making restoration into the jobs market challenging for many. We commit to fair trials, speedier justice, better systems of rehabilitation for prisoners, and an end to the dual role of the Lord Advocate. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
302 0 obj
<<
