347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (The NHS is a treasured institution, but under current conditions, it's crumbling. Waiting lists stretch for miles, doctors are fleeing, and our vulnerable are left in despair. Independence is the only way to take full control and rebuild a healthcare system that puts patients first.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (We will invest in training more doctors and nurses in order to address staff shortages, and will invest the estate and infrastructure of small practices within the NHS. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (Social care for our elderly and disabled must be integrated with the NHS, not treated as an afterthought. We'll boost carer allowances, expand home care services. Palliative care will be a priority, with heavy investment to support the terminally ill without the shadow of state-sanctioned death.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
350 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (We will move quickly to remove the benefit cliffs that disincentivise workers from doing more hours or taking on more responsibility at work. No one on in-work benefits should be penalised for earning more. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 212 0 R
/E (Most core benefits \(Universal Credit, tax credits, Jobseeker's Allowance, much disability support\) and the full income tax machinery \(allowances, savings/dividends, HMRC administration\) remain reserved to Westminster. Devolution allows top-ups and new Scottish benefits \(like Scottish Child Payment\), but not a complete redesign of the entire tax-benefit system.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
