390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (Having won a democratic mandate for independence, as soon as the ground as been laid, we will declare the 1707 Acts of Union to be null and void, and announce that Scotland has regained her independence.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (If this approach has the support of the Scottish people, but is met with resistance by the British state, then the Scottish people will be within their rights peacefully to take to the streets. This is not a route that we want to take, but we are conscious that our birthright will not be returned to us on a plate.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (Critical to this strategy is disengagement with the institutions of the British state. It's an approach that each of us can adopt now. It's one that creates consequences for the British state to which it must respond.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (While the Independence Movement does not need to be united around questions of its vision for an independent Scotland or around political ideology, it is essential that we share a common strategic approach. The Alliance is one of the most promising initiatives in this direction, and our decision to align with it is taken for the sole purpose of uniting our efforts with fellow patriots seeking that Scotland once again be free.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
